{
  "_comment": "WHAT PAID COMFYUI PARTNER NODES COST, and therefore what we charge for them. Edit this file and redeploy the agent — no code change, which is the whole point of it being data. Prices are ComfyUI credits, taken from https://docs.comfy.org/tutorials/partner-nodes/pricing (~100 credits = $1). They DO drift; re-check this file against that page when Comfy announces changes, and against the account's actual invoice.",

  "_comment_safety": "THE DEFAULT FOR AN UNKNOWN PAID NODE IS TO REFUSE, never to charge nothing. A partner node this file does not price would otherwise run on the publisher's prepaid balance for free, and the first sign would be the invoice. `providers[].match` is how a node is recognised as billable at all: if a class name matches a provider prefix but no model entry prices it, the run is refused with a message naming the class — which is a two-minute edit here rather than a silent leak.",

  "_comment_matching": "A node is priced in two steps: its class_type is matched against a provider prefix, then the node's own inputs are searched for a string naming one of that provider's models. No model match falls back to the provider's `default_model`. This is deliberately loose about exact class names, because Comfy renames and adds nodes faster than this file can track — a provider prefix is far more stable than any one class name.",

  "version": 1,
  "updated": "2026-09-10",

  "credits_per_usd": 100,

  "_comment_markup": "What we charge on top of what Comfy charges us. It is not profit-taking so much as insurance: the prices below are a snapshot, Comfy's are live, and a table that has drifted low bills us the difference on every run.",
